  "method": "Identical package-lock and installed dependency graph; renderer built with electron-vite (renderer target) on each revision and measured with scripts/check-renderer-bundle.mjs accounting. The watcher dock and attach dialog closures exclude every entry, workbench and detached-chat chunk, and the attach dialog also excludes chunks it shares with the dock.",
  "notes": [
    "foundation: watcher event and result validators join the deferred server-event schema chunk; 841 bytes reach each first-load route.",
    "renderer: eager wiring is the link index, the per-chat dock record, the chip, the dock and attach hosts, the live-phase store, the timeline divider and check model and the composer lock; the dock UI and the attach dialog stay in WatcherDock-* and WatcherAttachDialog-*.",
    "entryCss grows by 70 bytes and stays within its existing ceiling.",
    "Small changes on unrelated deferred chunks are import metadata for helpers (dialog shell, elapsed timing) that Rollup now shares with the watcher chunks.",
    "After merging v0.0.73 (e165a0a), mergedMainBaselineBytes is that revision and mergedBytes the merged branch, built from the same package-lock. Only deferredTasksViewJavaScript needed more room: v0.0.73 measures exactly its 21,126-byte budget and the Work tab nesting adds 6 bytes."
